<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Trigger Inversion Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Candidates are ranked by <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 BABI DEFENSE FOR LLMs ‣ Inverting Trojans in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=40</annotation></semantics></math>).
For singletons (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>), the ground-truth token “<span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">seriously</span>” appears among the top-5 across poisoned models (Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Trigger Inversion Results ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Inverting Trojans in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
For bi-token sequences (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j{=}2</annotation></semantics></math>), “<span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tell seriously</span>” is consistently recovered among the top-8 for <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">d_0.5</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">d_0.8</span>, and <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">c_7</span> (Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.3 Trigger Inversion Results ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Inverting Trojans in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
For tri-token sequences (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>), the fragment “<span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tell me seriously</span>” ranks among the highest candidates for <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">d_0.5</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">c_5</span> (Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.3 Trigger Inversion Results ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Inverting Trojans in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
